{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WWj7h5y6nSP6wiioikyPRB","type":"tool_result","content":"# IT-020-3:2013 NOSS Related Knowledge Extract\n\nFor validation use only. Derived from NOSS CoCU source documents.\n\n## CU2: Computer System Maintenance (Penyelenggaraan Sistem Komputer)\n\n- K1: Types of maintenance — preventive (scheduled) vs corrective (fault-driven)\n- K2: Maintenance tools and materials (compressed air, IPA, anti-static brush, thermal paste)\n- K3: Thermal management — thermal paste replacement procedure; fan inspection\n- K4: Software maintenance — OS updates, antivirus definitions, event log review, SMART data\n- K5: Maintenance report components — asset ID, tasks performed, parts used, sign-off\n\n## CU3: Computer System Repair (Pembaikan Sistem Komputer)\n\n- K1: Repair job order / change request — fields, assessment, escalation criteria\n- K2: Online troubleshooting — remote desktop, knowledge base, diagnostic scripts\n- K3: POST (Power-On Self-Test) — beep codes, fault indicators, diagnostic sequence\n- K4: Hardware fault diagnosis — PSU multimeter checks, RAM Memtest86, SMART for storage\n- K5: Computer status report — fault description, actions taken, parts used, test result\n\n## CU4: Server Installation (Pemasangan Pelayan)\n\n- K1: Server types — tower, rack-mount, blade; role and selection criteria\n- K2: RAID levels — RAID 0, 1, 5, 10; purpose, minimum drives, read/write behaviour\n- K3: Server rack installation — rack unit (U) sizing, cable management, power redundancy\n- K4: Server OS and software installation — driver order, role/feature activation, initial config\n- K5: Server functionality testing — POST, network ping, service verification, handover report","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2b23ae1-4af5-4599-99be-753e46a72a1f","uuid":"22948697-0707-46c1-9c43-29a7d1330d2f","timestamp":"2026-04-17T08:59:04.777Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# IT-020-3:2013 NOSS Related Knowledge Extract\n\nFor validation use only. Derived from NOSS CoCU source documents.\n\n## CU2: Computer System Maintenance (Penyelenggaraan Sistem Komputer)\n\n- K1: Types of maintenance — preventive (scheduled) vs corrective (fault-driven)\n- K2: Maintenance tools and materials (compressed air, IPA, anti-static brush, thermal paste)\n- K3: Thermal management — thermal paste replacement procedure; fan inspection\n- K4: Software maintenance — OS updates, antivirus definitions, event log review, SMART data\n- K5: Maintenance report components — asset ID, tasks performed, parts used, sign-off\n\n## CU3: Computer System Repair (Pembaikan Sistem Komputer)\n\n- K1: Repair job order / change request — fields, assessment, escalation criteria\n- K2: Online troubleshooting — remote desktop, knowledge base, diagnostic scripts\n- K3: POST (Power-On Self-Test) — beep codes, fault indicators, diagnostic sequence\n- K4: Hardware fault diagnosis — PSU multimeter checks, RAM Memtest86, SMART for storage\n- K5: Computer status report — fault description, actions taken, parts used, test result\n\n## CU4: Server Installation (Pemasangan Pelayan)\n\n- K1: Server types — tower, rack-mount, blade; role and selection criteria\n- K2: RAID levels — RAID 0, 1, 5, 10; purpose, minimum drives, read/write behaviour\n- K3: Server rack installation — rack unit (U) sizing, cable management, power redundancy\n- K4: Server OS and software installation — driver order, role/feature activation, initial config\n- K5: Server functionality testing — POST, network ping, service verification, handover report","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
